hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1139","Muhammad bin Ali bin Mahrez told us, on the authority of Yaqoub, meaning Ibn Ibrahim bin Saad, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He told me Hakim bin Hakim bin Abbad bin Hunaif, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Ali bin Al-Hussein told him that his father Al-Hussein bin Ali told him that His father, Ali bin Abi Talib, told him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Ali and Fatima at night, and said to us: “Get up.” So they prayed.” Then he returned to his house, and when the middle of the night had passed, he returned, but he did not listen to us at all, so he said: “Stand up and pray.” He said: So I got up, and I My eyes hurt, so I said: O Messenger of God, by God we do not pray except what God has ordained for us. Our souls are in the hands of God. If He wills, He will resurrect us. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away, striking his thigh with his hand, and saying: “Shall we pray except what God has decreed for us?” And the man was The most controversial thing is Surah Al-Kahf, verse 54."
"1140","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Hujain bin Al-Muthanna Abu Umair told us, Al-Layth, meaning Ibn Saad, told us, on the authority of Uqail, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, that Hassan bin Ali, narrated to him, such and such. Ibn Rafi’ said to us: Indeed, Hassan bin Ali, narrated to him, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to him and Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Aren’t you praying?” So I said: O Messenger of God, our lives are in the hands of God, so if He wishes to send us, He will send us. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed when I said That, and he did not return anything to me. Then I heard him as he was turning away, striking his thigh, and saying: And man was the most contentious of all things. Surat Al-Kahf, verse 54."
